id: pm-rust-ci-v2
title: Apply Fleet CI v2 quick PR and full deep tiers
description: "Companion pm-cli-website-dyhg. Preserve required Rust platform checks and the release aggregate, split quick PR work from full deep gates, retain complete coverage thresholds, and certify routing and depth controls."
type: Task
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[3]: ci,"gh:unbraind/pm-rust#173",performance
created_at: "2026-11-16T05:26:56.154Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-16T07:30:35.274Z"
author: codex-sol
acceptance_criteria: Preserve all required contexts and original checks; prove deterministic quick depth and bounded jobs; record measured CI and release claim.
comments[12]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-16T05:26:58.811Z",codex-sol,"Initial audit: required contexts verified as Rust ubuntu-latest, Rust macos-latest, Rust windows-latest and Release gate aggregate; CodeQL is not required. No existing open CI v2 item found. Plan: quick deterministic corpora and property counts; parallel Linux release components with an always-running strict aggregate; full npm/Bun and OS gates in deep. Preserve release workflows and verifier scripts."
  "2026-11-16T05:35:40.449Z",codex-sol,"Baseline run 43729555388: Rust execution Linux 790s, macOS 863s, Windows 1364s; full aggregates Linux npm 1610s, Bun 2376s, macOS 2073s, Windows 3236s. Slow Linux targets: claim/release 180.71s, orientation 138.80s, pagination 108.38s, search/collections 83.77s. Implemented two disjoint platform target shards, fail-closed required aggregates, parallel Linux quick release components, unchanged full-scope 100% LLVM coverage, deterministic quick property prefixes and kind-preserving focused crash replays. Deep keeps complete original gates and unscaled latency budgets. Local setup is user-space and locked; cold WAN tool bootstrap and ptrace still need runner evidence."
  "2026-11-16T05:42:58.787Z",codex-sol,"Initial local validation passed: cargo check and clippy on all targets/features; fmt; typed harness typecheck/lint; two partition/identity fixtures; 12 documentation contracts; unchanged changelog; strict YAML with duplicate-key rejection; shell parsing. Strict health passes with a clean HOME and installed merge drivers: the inherited-home extension skew was local configuration, not a repository defect. Touched quick-depth Rust suites are still running; no full local suite or coverage claim. Publishing early for hosted validation."
  "2026-11-16T05:45:07.142Z",codex-sol,"Opened PR https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rust/pull/173 at d204834. ci-deep branch dispatch was attempted and refused HTTP 404 because the workflow is absent on main; no workaround attempted. Initial push completed 05:43:05 UTC; CI observation is bounded to 30 minutes after the last push. Strict health passes with clean HOME after merge-driver installation; inherited-home extension skew was local configuration."
  "2026-11-16T05:51:41.002Z",codex-sol,"Hosted first-run policy passed in 30s created-to-completed, quality in 70s, crash harness in 147s. Rust shards and coverage are still running. Follow-up preserves deep watchdog scale only in parent/child crash tests, with finite-positive/integer timer validation; product timeout option bounds remain unchanged. Added physical cleanup-fsync cases for both mutation operations (2/2 local pass, 109.67s) to retain cleanup phase coverage when quick omits the exhaustive ordinal sweep. Sampled capability-subset matrices retain each capability granted and absent."
  "2026-11-16T05:55:17.868Z",codex-sol,"Local crash tests at quick depth and watchdog scale 3 passed 37 with one intentional exhaustive-corpus skip in 514.651s; the two added cleanup-fsync cases independently passed in 109.670s. Harness typecheck/lint, shell parsing and diff whitespace checks pass after watchdog edits. Hosted Linux shards and both macOS shards have passed on d204834; Windows and unchanged-threshold coverage remain in progress. Broad local touched-target run is progressing under contention; no full suite was started."
  "2026-11-16T05:56:17.391Z",codex-sol,"Stopped the broad local touched-target run after roughly 20 minutes of shared-host contention. Admission 12/12, capability 6/6, depth fixture 1/1 and adapter 13/13 passed; pagination completed 32/33, including its modified property test, without failure before termination. The remaining unchanged mixed-status cross-product was still running. This is incomplete local evidence, not a pass. Running only the changed test functions plus workflow contracts next; hosted Linux quick target shards already passed."
  "2026-11-16T06:08:20.637Z",codex-sol,"First PR run 43812108627 at d204834 completed successfully, including all required checks and unchanged 100% coverage thresholds. The unsharded coverage exceeded the 15-minute target, so coverage now uses two disjoint target shards and native LLVM raw-profile union behind the required aggregate. Both real merge fixtures passed: native per-file counter equality and the actual Cargo separate-target/mapping-rebuild flow, including corruption/identity refusals. No percentage averaging, source exclusion or threshold changes. Full release recipe is preserved; its harness lint now also checks the new CI helpers."
  "2026-11-16T06:10:05.221Z",codex-sol,"First PR run 43812108627 at d204834 passed all required checks and unchanged 100% coverage. Per-job created-to-completed seconds: policy 30; changes 8; quality 70; crash 147; Linux Rust shards 422/500; macOS 607/390; Windows 854/711; unsharded coverage 1101; required Rust Linux/macOS/Windows aggregates 10/102/16; release aggregate 134. Aggregate creation follows dependencies, so these exclude predecessor time. Quick target ranking: orientation 194.12s, claims 175.61s, search 120.87s, pagination 107.09s, close 75.90s, library 31.17s. Coverage sharding addresses the measured target miss; 2/2 native/Cargo union fixtures and 25/25 depth/workflow contracts passed through pm, with final clippy/fmt and harness typecheck/lint passing."
  "2026-11-16T06:27:51.681Z",codex-sol,"Final implementation cce2f8f, run 43814943607: all CI jobs and all four required checks passed; CodeQL passed. Created-to-completed seconds: Tracker, identity and documentation 28; changes 7; Quick release quality 55; Quick crash harness 200; Quick Rust ubuntu-latest shard 1 426; Quick Rust windows-latest shard 1 846; Quick coverage shard 2 480; Quick Rust windows-latest shard 2 644; Quick Rust macos-latest shard 2 339; Quick Rust ubuntu-latest shard 2 373; Quick Rust macos-latest shard 1 450; Quick coverage shard 1 615; Quick exact coverage union 91; Release gate aggregate 6; Rust windows-latest 6; Rust ubuntu-latest 7; Rust macos-latest 5. Exact union restored 4226 original profiles; both required merge fixtures passed and lines/functions/regions/branches stayed 100%. Every quick job was below 15 minutes. Deep remains unverified: dispatch 404; cold user-space bootstrap, ptrace and local latency need the first deep run. No local full-depth suite ran. Broad local pagination was incomplete at 32/33 after roughly 20 minutes, with its changed property test passed separately. Claims will be released without closing."
  "2026-11-16T07:22:40.546Z",codex-sol,"Review round K: verify the requested coverage portability and independent-oracle findings, binding inventory, or property cap contract as applicable; add focused regressions and run the required package gates. Keep this item in progress and release the claim after recording results. No review-thread mutations or merges."
  "2026-11-16T07:30:28.910Z",codex-sol,"Round K: PRRT_kwDOTwgMRs63y74W verified and fixed. Extracted property_cases_for with explicit full count, depth and cap text; runtime behavior still honors positive caps, ignores invalid/zero caps, and preserves full/quick defaults. The contract now tests explicit no-cap, cap 10, larger cap, invalid, zero, negative and overflow inputs without changing the environment. Required pm test gate passed: cargo fmt --all -- --check; cargo check --locked; cargo clippy --locked --all-targets --all-features -- -D warnings; env -u PROPTEST_CASES cargo test --locked --test ci_depth_contract; PROPTEST_CASES=10 cargo test --locked --test ci_depth_contract (2 tests passed in each configuration); node --test scripts/crash-ci-contract.test.mts scripts/crash-coverage-union.test.mts; git diff --check. The first Node invocation has 3 passed and 2 opt-in skips; a separate PM_TEST_COVERAGE_MERGE=required node --test scripts/crash-coverage-union.test.mts passed both real LLVM union contracts, and cargo test --locked --test release_pipeline_contract passed all 24. No required merge evidence remains skipped. Project test-result tracking is disabled; this comment retains results. No thread mutations. Releasing in progress for orchestrator verification."
